 "title": "How to Write Copy in Someone's Specific Voice",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "This video explains three tactical steps to ghostwrite copy in another person's unique voice. The creator shares how building a story bible, analyzing voice samples, and using an anti-AI checklist help produce authentic content.",
 "key_points": [
  "Step 1: Create a story bible covering the person's upbringing, mistakes, failures, goals, and dreams so the writer has an accurate picture of their life.",
  "Step 2: Build a voice skill by transcribing podcasts, YouTube videos, or Instagram videos, then feed the transcripts to Claude to analyze writing patterns.",
  "Step 3: Create an anti-AI checklist to filter out common AI 'isms' and have the AI tool self-check the draft before returning it."
 ],
 "content": "How I write for top 1% entrepreneurs at 20 ($200k/mo) [Speaker 1]: So you work with Hormozi, Shelby Sapp, Noah Kagan. People don't know that a lot of the content they're consuming from those people is actually written by you. So how do you make sure to write good copy in their specific voice? [Speaker 2]: So the first step is I just consume a lot of their content. That's why I'm really picky with who I work with. I don't want to be brainwashed by people who I don't think have an accurate reality on life. But like tactically there's three things I do. #1 Story Bible. So the first step is I create a story bible. If we think of like training someone, if we want someone to write for you, they need to have a full accurate picture on your entire life story, your upbringing, your mistakes, your failures, your goals, dreams, everything. #2 Voice skill. The second thing that we build is a voice skill. So basically what I'll do is I'll transcribe podcasts, YouTube videos, for Shelby it was Instagram videos, yeah, I'll transcribe a ton of it and basically feed that to Claude and have it analyze the patterns between how she writes. #3 Anti-AI Checklist. And then the third thing that I'll do is I'll create an anti-AI checklist. So whenever you write with Claude or any other AI tool, inevitably there are like isms that, you know, make it seem like AI and so we just have it run this checklist of like don't use these things and so we have it write a draft and then we have it use the anti-AI skill to self check itself before it gives it back to me. And so when you have those three things you're able to write in someone's voice. [Speaker 1]: Well dude, how do I sign up? [Speaker 2]: revenuemediaelab.com Text shown on screen: #1 Story Bible, #2 Voice skill, #3 Anti-AI Checklist, revenuemediaelab.com. Instagram reel/post by Jay Yang. Text / caption: Hi, if you’re new here my name is Jay Yang. When I was 15, I googled “how to make money online”. I stumbled into this little-known skill called copywriting and became obsessed. • what motivates us to take action? • can we influence those motivations? • how can words influence people? Learning that one skill has gotten me everything I’ve wanted out of life (except for a wife lol) • landed dream jobs • signed dream clients • built a 500k+ audience • wrote 2 best-selling books • built a 7-figure copywriting agency I suck at many things. I can’t swing a golf club. I can’t dance. I don’t know anything about the latest news and trends. BUT… I truly believe I am the best damn social media copywriter in the game. X posts. LinkedIn posts. IG carousels. Ads. Wanna learn more about working with me? Comment “COPY” and let’s chat 🤝",
